cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-dup-dev: duplicate adjudication for pharmacovigilance reports"
abstract: >-
  A duplicate adjudication pipeline for pharmacovigilance adverse event reports,
  with the evaluation framework used to measure its performance. Report pairs
  flagged as suspected duplicates by an upstream candidate-generation method are
  classified as Duplicates, Otherwise related, Unrelated, or Abstain by a
  transparent rule-based decision logic combining rarity-based matching
  evidence, structured and clinical-date inconsistency signals, LLM-derived
  narrative signals, and explicit inter-report links.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Norén"
    given-names: "G. Niklas"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4595-230X"
    # TODO confirm affiliation string before publishing.
    affiliation: "Uppsala Monitoring Centre"
version: 1.0.0
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - pharmacovigilance
  - duplicate detection
  - record linkage
  - adverse drug reactions
  - large language models

